l: after task8, does handler/doing.go still import git? Item 5 says \"commit 由 pi 在每个 task 成功后立即执行\". And `commitDoingResults` uses `git.New`. That whole function would be removed or moved. So handler/doing.go should no longer import git. But what about `ensureGitInitialized`/`ensureGitUserConfigured` which also use git? Those are also in handler/doing.go. They might stay (git init is still needed?) or move. Hmm, this is ambiguous. `ensureGitInitialized` uses `exec.Command(\"git\", \"init\")` (shell git, not internal/git package). `commitDoingResults` uses `internal/git` package (`git.New`, `git.NewAutoCommitter`). \n\nItem 5 says \"commit 由 pi 在每个 task 成功后立即执行（复用 mark_task_success_skill 模式）\". So the Go-side `commitDoingResults` using `internal/git` should be removed. But `ensureGitInitialized` (shell git init) might remain or move. This is ambiguous. To avoid false failure, I'll only check that handler/doing.go does NOT import `internal/executor` (unambiguous — the executor package is deleted) and does NOT import `internal/parser` (unambiguous — parser deleted). For git, since `internal/git` is deleted (it's in the 6 packages), ANY import of `internal/git` would break the build, so `go build` already covers it. So I don't need a separate grep for git. Similarly for parser/executor — the build covers it. \n\nWait, that's a key insight: since the 6 packages are DELETED, any remaining import of them breaks `go build`. So the \"packages deleted\" check + \"go build succeeds\" check TOGETHER cover \"all consumers migrated\". So I don't need separate grep checks for handler imports. The build is the real gate.\n\nSo my structure simplifies:\n1. `go build ./cmd/rick` succeeds (real gate for migration).\n2. 6 packages deleted (structural).\n3. tools_doing_check.go/tools_plan_check.go deleted (structural, also covered by build if cmd/tools.go still references them → build fails).\n4. helper.py exists + functional.\n5. dry-run normal + boundary (dependency order + skip).\n6