gDryRun` doesn't call config.LoadConfig. It calls `workspace.GetRickDir()` (cwd-based) and `builder.NewPIBuilder().SaveDoingPrompt(...)`.\n\nBut wait, `SaveDoingPrompt` calls `prompt.LoadLoopsContext` and `prompt.LoadSkillsContext` from rickDir. In a temp dir, `.rick/loops` and `.rick/skills` won't exist. Let me check whether those functions gracefully handle missing dirs.\n\nLet me check the prompt package. Actually, task7 created `jobs_dir` with `dream_dir` but didn't create `loops`/`skills`/`domain`. And it worked for dream/learning/ctrl. For doing dry-run, we need `loops` and `skills` to not error. Let me check `LoadLoopsContext` and `LoadSkillsContext`.\n\nAlso, the doing prompt template references `{{doing_loop_content}}` which is loaded via `renderDoingLoop` → `prompt.LoadCoreSkills([]string{\"doing_loop\"})` which reads embedded templates. That should be fine.\n\nLet me check the prompt package functions and also whether the plan dir needs task*.md files.\n\nLet me look at the prompt package.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_Tu5QJvhZ3oen9swul4uE1647","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && ls -R internal/prompt/ | head -80"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_01_sECaGQDirn5NIOEWX7Ou3286","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && grep -rn \"func LoadLoopsContext\\|func LoadSkillsContext\\|func LoadCoreSkills\\|func EnsurePromptsDir\\|func NewPromptManager\\|func GenerateDoingPromptFile\\|func (p \\*PromptManager)\" internal/prompt/"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":8322,"output":1357,"cacheRead":45056,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":1192,"totalTokens":54735,"cost":{"input":0.00362007,"output":0.00118059,"cacheRead":0.00016332800000000002,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.004963988}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786911942331,"responseId":"465a469e-ce27-4b22-a594-9aebe96c6067","rawStopReason":"too